IMPORT prelude

-- Saint Andrew's Mission Hospital Ordinance 1934 (Singapore) -- who may be a member of the Corporation and on what subscription
-- (ss 7-9), what the Corporation may pay its members (s 6), who may stand for the Board (ss 18, 22), the annual and special
-- meetings members can call (ss 29, 30), changing the rules (ss 33, 34), where the property goes on a winding up (s 35), and
-- the meeting rules in the Second Schedule (rules 1, 2, 4, 9, 14, 15).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SAMHO1934.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The
-- latest amendment annotated in the body is [40/2019] on s 35 (the Legislative History lists Act 40 of 2019, the Supreme Court
-- of Judicature (Amendment) Act 2019, in force 2 January 2021); s 36 carries [7/97].
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0247 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The people it touches are the hospital's subscribers and members, so this row takes membership,
-- the money rule, elections, meetings, rule changes and winding up. Not encoded: incorporation and vesting of the Erskine Road
-- land (ss 2-4), the objects (s 5), the named Founder, Patrons and first officers (ss 10-13, 20-22 second sentences), the
-- Treasurer, auditor and Chaplain (ss 13-17), the Bishop's control of medical officers and nursing sisters (s 25), the Board's
-- powers and committees (ss 26-28, 31), the First Schedule endowments, and Second Schedule rules not listed above.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Saint Andrew's Mission Hospital Ordinance 1934 -- members`

§§ `7 -- classes of member`

-- s 7(2): "The persons named in the Register of Subscribers abovementioned, and every person who shall have subscribed in the
-- aggregate the sum of $500 ... shall be entitled to be members for life or in the case of a firm or corporation till the
-- dissolution of such firm or corporation and shall be called permanent members." (The preamble: the Register of Subscribers
-- holds "every person (firm and corporation) who has made a donation of not less than $500 to the building fund".)
-- Reading "the sum of $500" as "at least $500" is an inference.
GIVEN `named in the Register of Subscribers` IS A BOOLEAN, `aggregate subscribed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to be a permanent member` IF
    `named in the Register of Subscribers` OR `aggregate subscribed` AT LEAST 500

-- s 7(3): "Every person who in any calendar year shall have subscribed the sum of $12 (twelve dollars) shall be entitled to be
-- a member for the residue of that year, and the next following year and shall be called an ordinary member."
-- So a $12 subscription in year Y covers Y and Y + 1. Reading "$12" as "at least $12" is an inference.
GIVEN `subscribed in the year` IS A NUMBER, `the year of subscription` IS A NUMBER, `the year asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to be an ordinary member` IF
        `subscribed in the year` AT LEAST 12
    AND `the year asked about` AT LEAST `the year of subscription`
    AND `the year asked about` AT MOST `the year of subscription` PLUS 1

-- s 7(1): members of the Board "shall be members of the Corporation"; the Board "may appoint, with their consent" permanent,
-- ordinary and honorary members. s 8(1): the register holds those "who are qualified and consent to become members".
-- s 8(2): a member who wishes to retire "shall signify such desire in writing to the Secretary and thereupon his name shall be
-- removed". s 9: "The right of membership is not transferable or transmissible and shall cease upon a member ceasing to be a
-- member by death or otherwise."
GIVEN `sits on the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `qualifies for a class` IS A BOOLEAN, `consents` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `retired in writing to the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN, `has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a member of the Corporation` IF
        (NOT `has died`)
    AND (NOT `retired in writing to the Secretary`)
    AND (`sits on the Board` OR (`qualifies for a class` AND `consents`))

§§ `6 -- what the Corporation may pay a member`

-- s 6: income "shall be applied solely towards the promotion of the objects" and "no portion thereof shall be paid or transferred
-- directly or indirectly by way of dividend, bonus or otherwise howsoever by way of profits to the members". Proviso: this does
-- not prevent payment "in good faith" of (i) remuneration to an officer, servant or member "in return for services actually
-- rendered", (ii) interest on money borrowed from a member, or (iii) to a donor or nominee, an annuity "by way of annual interest
-- guaranteed by the Corporation on the amount of such gift during a period not exceeding the life of the donor or such nominee".
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `a dividend`
    `a bonus out of profits`
    `pay for services actually rendered`
    `interest on a loan from the member`
    `an annuity on a gift for the donor's life`
    `an annuity on a gift beyond the donor's life`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment, `made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment to a member is allowed` IF
    `made in good faith` AND
        CONSIDER `the payment`
        WHEN `pay for services actually rendered` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `interest on a loan from the member` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an annuity on a gift for the donor's life` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `18, 22 -- the Board and who may stand for it`

-- s 18: the Board consists of "the President, the Vice-President, the Treasurer, 8 nominated members, 2 professional members
-- and at least 7 but not more than 15 elective members".
GIVEN `elective members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of elective members is lawful` IF
    `elective members` AT LEAST 7 AND `elective members` AT MOST 15

GIVEN `elective members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the size of the Board` MEANS 3 PLUS 8 PLUS 2 PLUS `elective members`

-- s 22: elective members are elected at the annual general meeting "from amongst the members of the Corporation but no person
-- shall be eligible for election whilst holding any salaried office under the Corporation". s 23: they are "eligible for
-- re-election".
GIVEN `a member of the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a salaried office under the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for election to the Board` IF
    `a member of the Corporation` AND (NOT `holds a salaried office under the Corporation`)

§§ `29, 30 -- annual and special meetings`

-- s 29: the annual general meeting "shall be held annually not later than the month of April in each year".
GIVEN `month of the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annual general meeting is in time` IF
    `month of the meeting` AT MOST 4

-- s 30: the Board "may at any time and shall on a requisition signed by not less than 10 members of the Corporation stating the
-- objects of such requisition summon a special meeting ... to be held not less than 3 weeks and not later than 6 weeks after the
-- receipt of such requisition. If they neglect to do so within 14 days after the receipt of any such requisition, the
-- requisitionists may summon such meeting."
GIVEN `members who signed` IS A NUMBER, `states its objects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board must summon a special meeting` IF
    `members who signed` AT LEAST 10 AND `states its objects`

GIVEN `days after receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the special meeting date is lawful` IF
    `days after receipt` AT LEAST 21 AND `days after receipt` AT MOST 42

-- Reading "within 14 days" as "the requisitionists may act from day 15" is an inference.
GIVEN `members who signed` IS A NUMBER, `states its objects` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Board summoned it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requisitionists may summon the meeting themselves` IF
        `the Board must summon a special meeting` `members who signed` `states its objects`
    AND (NOT `the Board summoned it`)
    AND `days since receipt` GREATER THAN 14

§§ `33, 34 -- changing the rules`

-- s 33: rules may be revoked, altered or added to by the Board "provided that due notice shall have been given to the members of
-- the Board" and the change "is approved by a majority of not less than two-thirds of the members voting on the question".
-- s 34: no change to the Second Schedule rules "shall come into operation until the same shall have been approved by the
-- Minister and shall have been published in the Gazette".
GIVEN `due notice given` IS A BOOLEAN, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes cast` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule change is carried by the Board` IF
    `due notice given` AND `votes for` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `votes cast` TIMES 2

GIVEN `due notice given` IS A BOOLEAN, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes cast` IS A NUMBER,
      `approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule change is in operation` IF
        `the rule change is carried by the Board` `due notice given` `votes for` `votes cast`
    AND `approved by the Minister`
    AND `published in the Gazette`

§§ `35 -- winding up`

-- s 35: the Board may wind up "with the sanction of a special general meeting of the members of the Corporation called for the
-- purpose". What remains after debts "shall not be paid or distributed amongst the members of the Corporation or any of them, but
-- shall be given and transferred to some missionary association, society or institution of the Church of England within the
-- Diocese of Singapore having objects similar or in part similar", chosen "by a majority of three-fourths of the Board of
-- Management, with the approval of the Society for the Propagation of the Gospel, and in default thereof by the General Division
-- of the High Court".
GIVEN `the Board resolves` IS A BOOLEAN, `a special general meeting sanctions it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may be wound up` IF
    `the Board resolves` AND `a special general meeting sanctions it`

DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the members`
    `a Church of England mission in the Diocese with similar objects`
    `a Church of England mission outside the Diocese`
    `a secular charity with similar objects`
    `a mission of another church in Singapore`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surplus may go to` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a Church of England mission in the Diocese with similar objects` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Three-fourths "of the Board of Management" -- the whole Board, not those voting (contrast s 33). Reading it as three-fourths of
-- the Board's membership is an inference.
GIVEN `Board members in favour` IS A NUMBER, `Board size` IS A NUMBER, `the Society approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board chooses the recipient` IF
    `Board members in favour` TIMES 4 AT LEAST `Board size` TIMES 3 AND `the Society approves`

GIVEN `Board members in favour` IS A NUMBER, `Board size` IS A NUMBER, `the Society approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the High Court chooses the recipient` IF
    NOT `the Board chooses the recipient` `Board members in favour` `Board size` `the Society approves`

§§ `Second Schedule -- meetings`

-- Rule 1: "The quorum for a general meeting shall be 10 persons being members or representatives of members".
-- Rule 2: "An advertisement giving 10 days' previous notice published in the Gazette and in 2 English and one Chinese daily
-- newspapers published in Singapore shall be sufficient notice of a meeting." (Sufficient, not required.)
-- Rule 4: voting is by show of hands "but 5 members present may demand a poll".
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` AT LEAST 10

GIVEN `days of notice` IS A NUMBER, `in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN, `English dailies` IS A NUMBER, `Chinese dailies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advertisement is sufficient notice` IF
        `days of notice` AT LEAST 10
    AND `in the Gazette`
    AND `English dailies` AT LEAST 2
    AND `Chinese dailies` AT LEAST 1

GIVEN `members demanding` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a poll must be taken` IF
    `members demanding` AT LEAST 5

-- Rule 9: "5 members of the Board shall be a quorum"; notice "at least 7 days before such meeting, unless urgent circumstances
-- require shorter notice; but the proceedings of any meeting shall not be invalidated by any irregularity in respect of such
-- notice".
GIVEN `Board members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Board meeting is quorate` IF
    `Board members present` AT LEAST 5

-- Rules 14, 15: the Executive Committee is the President, Vice-President and Treasurer and "not less than 5 or more than 7 other
-- members of the Board", "so that at least 2 nominated members ... at least 2 elective members ... and one professional member"
-- sit on it. Rule 17: "until otherwise determined by the Board, 4 shall be a quorum".
GIVEN `nominated on it` IS A NUMBER, `elective on it` IS A NUMBER, `professional on it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Executive Committee is properly constituted` IF
        `nominated on it` PLUS `elective on it` PLUS `professional on it` AT LEAST 5
    AND `nominated on it` PLUS `elective on it` PLUS `professional on it` AT MOST 7
    AND `nominated on it` AT LEAST 2
    AND `elective on it` AT LEAST 2
    AND `professional on it` AT LEAST 1
